The NEH has recently supported a dedicated scholarly institute on “Imagination and Imaginal Worlds in Buddhism,” explicitly bringing together Buddhist literature, ritual, meditation, art and theories of mind–world creation. This confirms that the Buddhist-imaginal side of your intersection is becoming a recognisable academic research area.

